{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779564532,"nonce":"gL8ROs9vudcgky3BsVlAyg3GlaY=","title":"Studio: expose built-in graph templates as subgraph components","message":"## Summary\n\nExpose Feedbax-distributed graph templates as reusable subgraph components in Studio, either in the existing components sidebar or in a sibling Templates tab in the same sidebar.\n\n## Context\n\nThis child comes from umbrella `07c0ec9`. Feedbax is moving built-in composites away from backend-special classes (`SimpleFeedback`, `SimpleStagedNetwork`) and toward canonical `GraphSpec` template/spec factories. Those templates need a product surface so users can instantiate and inspect predefined subgraphs rather than only leaf components.\n\n## Initial template catalog from `feature/graph-templates`\n\nThe current branch is expected to introduce at least these base templates:\n\n- `feedbax.templates.network` / Network: recurrent network as an executable `GraphSpec` subgraph.\n- `feedbax.templates.simple_feedback` / Simple Feedback Loop: feedback channel, controller, efferent path, and mechanics loop.\n\nExisting CDE preset template graphs should be reviewed as part of the same catalog, but some are display/documentation templates with non-executable nodes. The UI should distinguish executable templates from display-only/documentation templates.\n\n## Product requirements\n\n- Template entries should be visible as predefined subgraphs, not mixed ambiguously with leaf components.\n- The sidebar can either add a Templates tab next to Components or clearly group templates in the existing component library.\n- Instantiating a template should create a subgraph/component node with the template graph and default UI state.\n- Users should be able to enter/open the subgraph immediately and edit/lower it like any other authored subgraph.\n- Base distributed templates should carry stable ids, labels, category, description, executable/display kind, parameters/defaults, and template graph payload.\n- User-defined/lowered subgraphs can later be saved as templates, but this issue is about the finite catalog shipped with base Studio.\n\n## Done criteria\n\n- Studio lists the Feedbax-provided graph templates from provider/registry data, not hard-coded frontend-only constants.\n- Network and Simple Feedback Loop can be instantiated from the template catalog and round-trip as `GraphSpec`.\n- Display-only templates are visibly distinct from executable graph templates.\n- The template catalog remains compatible with the component registry and typed subgraph taxonomy work (`6116155`, `2f8dd61`).\n\nRelated: `07c0ec9`, `93f79f2`, `6116155`, `2f8dd61`.","files":null}]}